# Build context for the root Dockerfile (build:sync). Line 20 of that Dockerfile
# is `COPY . .`, so without this file everything in the workspace is uploaded to
# the daemon and baked into the build stage's layer cache.
#
# This became load-bearing rather than merely tidy when the `test` job's
# workspace mount changed from `:ro` to read-write (it had to: Maven's first act
# is to create target/, and the job could not previously do that). test,
# build:native and build:sync all run on the SAME shell-executor workspace, so
# target/ now really exists when build:sync runs -- and build:native leaves a
# ~128 MB `target/remote-fragment` in it. GitLab's default
# GIT_CLEAN_FLAGS=-ffdx would remove it, but this pipeline pins neither
# GIT_STRATEGY nor GIT_CLEAN_FLAGS, so relying on that is an unstated dependency
# on a GitLab default. Excluding it here does not depend on runner config.
#
# Keep .mvn/, mvnw, pom.xml, settings.xml and src/ -- the build stage runs
# `./mvnw -B -s settings.xml package` and needs all five.

# Maven output, including the native binary build:native leaves behind.
target/
*.class

# VCS + the sparse clone lint:deploy-manifest-drift makes of the generator repo.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.central-manifest/

# Local Maven repo, if anyone ever caches one under the workspace.
.m2/

# Pentest/report output (see the Makefile's pentest + sca targets).
out/

# Not consumed by this image: the nginx image builds from the `nginx/` context,
# and the k8s manifests/CI config are never read at build time.
nginx/
deploy/
hugmesh-deploy.yaml
.github/
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Secrets and local overrides must never reach the daemon.
.env
*.env

# IDE / OS metadata.
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
